[{:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-7627"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981529/assets/2ab9745cb9d157e566c101a6ca79514017903fa57eaf8725c846afd272c74f93.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the general equation of an ellipse centered at $(h,k)$ with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the ellipse is centered at $(3,-1),$ the horizontal radius has length $a=2,$ and the vertical radius has length $b=4.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{{2}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-(-1))^{2}}{{4}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(y+1)^{2}}{16} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-115310/selection/8fbd2d3f8fec30b8988b313ab55584eaf14bae431349fa2771dc259291903d20" :answer/id #uuid "238b4156-fe38-512b-8174-689e062953d5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(3,5)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115310/selection/a8d21c191bb52f35e36b7998de659bcfd3f034bae56d7de9f7b5454525c340d2" :answer/id #uuid "6d1de455-fa3c-55bb-9b6a-8ec1e3f8b163" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(0,4)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115310/selection/566c033cc670f2eeb576d333926890b0dcdb71cae9a92ce2d64ad76e8173074e" :answer/id #uuid "7d84c2b7-7e87-5003-a0ae-cf907011148a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(4,0)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115310/selection/c7d7f5865a04f287adfbc7ccac92458329d02c053e1fa27cc0df187ff8f49c48" :answer/id #uuid "4662b591-a4d4-5680-8213-224d41f4d23e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(0,-4)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115310/selection/85cb4fac0396602d43dca2c00e3ca71b29816b8e6c6a13d1cfa7f3ced25f7b78" :answer/id #uuid "897f2f6b-955d-5a90-b368-aafbe23fc778" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(0,2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115310/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "bb73f107-6494-54b1-8438-bfd8864c7ff9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-115310/selection/c7d7f5865a04f287adfbc7ccac92458329d02c053e1fa27cc0df187ff8f49c48" :answer-field/choices ["q-115310/selection/8fbd2d3f8fec30b8988b313ab55584eaf14bae431349fa2771dc259291903d20" "q-115310/selection/a8d21c191bb52f35e36b7998de659bcfd3f034bae56d7de9f7b5454525c340d2" "q-115310/selection/566c033cc670f2eeb576d333926890b0dcdb71cae9a92ce2d64ad76e8173074e" "q-115310/selection/c7d7f5865a04f287adfbc7ccac92458329d02c053e1fa27cc0df187ff8f49c48" "q-115310/selection/85cb4fac0396602d43dca2c00e3ca71b29816b8e6c6a13d1cfa7f3ced25f7b78"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-115310" :question/id #uuid "eb7c4e5a-23fb-5e2d-b89b-6f04ed6e4095" :question/math-academy-id "q-115310" :question/problem "What is the center of the ellipse $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{(y+4)^{2}}{25}=1?$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the general equation of an ellipse centered at $(h,k)$ with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn the given equation, we have $h=0$ and $k=-4,$ so the center is located at $(0,-4).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-115310/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a5028940-be34-56b7-8947-6129252f06a7"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-115310"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-278347/field-1/125f24f362f0f175d87ace55e97787e0f2f97a6fccef0ccb876df8350c2a07e3" :answer/id #uuid "d343ee0c-0bce-549f-a377-d82fee76ecc2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{(x-2)^2}{9}+\\frac{(y+3)^2}{36}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-278347/field-1/e7475ac25980f61d7ae92ccd6e264beb8c64549757a26838edccd0f3af11bf6f" :answer/id #uuid "629b8174-ce7b-5e6f-be8a-18285794a866" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{(x-2)^2}{9}+\\frac{(y+3)^2}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-278347/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "62b7ea3b-fcb6-5690-8365-0a52be1947eb" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-278347/field-1/125f24f362f0f175d87ace55e97787e0f2f97a6fccef0ccb876df8350c2a07e3" :answer-field/choices ["q-278347/field-1/125f24f362f0f175d87ace55e97787e0f2f97a6fccef0ccb876df8350c2a07e3" "q-278347/field-1/e7475ac25980f61d7ae92ccd6e264beb8c64549757a26838edccd0f3af11bf6f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-278347" :question/id #uuid "3f5db72a-42be-544f-badf-b1a3297e7c62" :question/math-academy-id "q-278347" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981529/assets/89914bff0203020e476acedc399cfdcc4a546bac9ee747f01951019e8d85c85d.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?\n\n{{field-1}}$=1$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the general equation of an ellipse centered at $(h,k)$ with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the ellipse is centered at $(2,-3),$ the horizontal radius has length $a=3,$ and the vertical radius has length $b=6.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{{3}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-(-3))^{2}}{{6}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{9}+\\frac{(y+3)^{2}}{36} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-278347/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "57e19ee3-db9a-58d7-8ca3-4e8801aee656"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-278347"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-278401/field-1/83c2285763389b0bc8b13e9777da06a48782d28e9c124603d3003cc4dc2e718a" :answer/id #uuid "9797b665-acfe-5ef3-ab9d-e451919b916e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "14" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-278401/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "fbde829e-e840-53ab-8dd2-2f44399375ff" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-278401/field-1/83c2285763389b0bc8b13e9777da06a48782d28e9c124603d3003cc4dc2e718a" :answer-field/choices ["q-278401/field-1/83c2285763389b0bc8b13e9777da06a48782d28e9c124603d3003cc4dc2e718a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-278401/field-2/6cf1ba8fcecf7ff74fcb48e7f39a2cabed6551908e76b1f229ada74cff9b7d1c" :answer/id #uuid "382ed5a1-6a4a-5d26-a33d-4491ffb005ed" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-278401/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "f3349205-1811-5815-9329-dbfa5f8bc11b" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-278401/field-2/6cf1ba8fcecf7ff74fcb48e7f39a2cabed6551908e76b1f229ada74cff9b7d1c" :answer-field/choices ["q-278401/field-2/6cf1ba8fcecf7ff74fcb48e7f39a2cabed6551908e76b1f229ada74cff9b7d1c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-278401" :question/id #uuid "1d364c20-40e0-58aa-a4d5-2b6f9f2f6ac4" :question/math-academy-id "q-278401" :question/problem "For the ellipse $\\frac{(x-6)^{2}}{49}+\\frac{(y+5)^{2}}{7}=1,$ find the lengths of its major and minor axes.\n\n$\\,$ The length of the major axis is \n{{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The length of the minor axis is \n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Remember that the general equation of an ellipse centered at $(h,k)$ with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn the given equation, we have $h=6$ and $k=-5,$ so the center is located at $(6,-5).$\n\nIn the given equation, we also have ${a}^{2}=49$ and ${b}^{2}=7.$\n\n- Since ${a}^{2}=49,$ the length of the horizontal radius must be $a=\\sqrt{49}=7.$\n\n- Since ${b}^{2}=7,$ the length of the vertical radius must be $b=\\sqrt{7}.$\n\nSo the semi-major axis has length $a=7,$ and the semi-minor axis has length $b=\\sqrt{7}.$\n\nTherefore, the major axis has length $2a=2\\cdot 7=14,$ and the minor axis has length $2b=2\\cdot \\sqrt{7}=2\\sqrt{7}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-278401/field-1" "q-278401/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a5028940-be34-56b7-8947-6129252f06a7"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-278401"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-278404/field-1/e326a281f601aec64d5dcce4921033c5f93cbf7f8b0a7a5809a9962dfadde666" :answer/id #uuid "0f8eccc3-9000-5479-b4e9-01c9d24a4c32" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "18" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-278404/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "c1426200-9694-5ad7-bfe1-25419619f01c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-278404/field-1/e326a281f601aec64d5dcce4921033c5f93cbf7f8b0a7a5809a9962dfadde666" :answer-field/choices ["q-278404/field-1/e326a281f601aec64d5dcce4921033c5f93cbf7f8b0a7a5809a9962dfadde666"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-278404/field-2/219833e72de92bafe4f4f5813822a337104a6b771fd9bf741ddcca8750ecab9e" :answer/id #uuid "78384db2-8f46-5cae-ae65-c8d138abb397" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-278404/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "8da93786-0b28-53b3-bcb9-b8154a490fe2" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-278404/field-2/219833e72de92bafe4f4f5813822a337104a6b771fd9bf741ddcca8750ecab9e" :answer-field/choices ["q-278404/field-2/219833e72de92bafe4f4f5813822a337104a6b771fd9bf741ddcca8750ecab9e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-278404" :question/id #uuid "f7a9731a-7828-547b-97be-92ff1076f487" :question/math-academy-id "q-278404" :question/problem "For the ellipse $\\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{8}+\\frac{(y+8)^{2}}{81}=1,$ find the lengths of its major and minor axes.\n\n$\\,$ The length of the major axis is \n{{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The length of the minor axis is \n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Remember that the general equation of an ellipse centered at $(h,k)$ with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn the given equation, we have $h=3$ and $k=-8,$ so the center is located at $(3,-8).$\n\nIn the given equation, we also have ${a}^{2}=8$ and ${b}^{2}=81.$\n\n- Since ${a}^{2}=8,$ the length of the horizontal radius must be $a=\\sqrt{8}=2\\sqrt{2}.$\n\n- Since ${b}^{2}=81,$ the length of the vertical radius must be $b=\\sqrt{81}=9.$\n\nSo the semi-major axis has length $b=9,$ and the semi-minor axis has length $a=2\\sqrt{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the major axis has length $2b=2\\cdot 9=18,$ and the minor axis has length $2a=2\\cdot 2\\sqrt{2}=4\\sqrt{2}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-278404/field-1" "q-278404/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a5028940-be34-56b7-8947-6129252f06a7"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-278404"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
